# Trivy ignore file — a ratchet, not an allowlist of comfort.
#
# Generated 2026-09-30 by tools/update-trivy-baseline.sh against the images that
# actually deploy. The CI job runs Trivy with --ignorefile .trivyignore and
# --exit-code 1, so this file makes the gate meaningful rather than permanently
# red: a NEW high or critical finding fails the build, and an entry here only
# acknowledges one that already existed.
#
# Why a baseline exists at all: at the time of writing the deployable images
# carried 254 high/critical findings across 154 distinct identifiers, the
# majority inherited from upstream base images and from a Spring Boot 3.2.5 /
# Tomcat 10.1.20 / Netty 4.1.109 / Jackson 2.15.4 stack. Removing them all in one
# change would mean merging an unpinned dependency upgrade with a CI change, so
# the two are separated deliberately.
#
# The debt is tracked, not forgotten. See the dependency-upgrade issue linked
# from the commit that introduced this file. Review cadence: monthly, and
# whenever a base image is rebuilt.
#
# Do not add an ID here without reading the finding. A fix being available is
# recorded as a comment on the tracking issue, not suppressed here.
#
# Format: one identifier per line, optionally followed by a comment. Review
# date: regenerate wholesale with tools/update-trivy-baseline.sh rather than
# hand-editing, so the file always matches a real scan.

